      "Both audit subagents dispatched this iteration (Convex/SQLite parity + webhook idempotency; security/injection + untested orchestration) returned CLEAN against current HEAD, and the fold scan found nothing unmerged (every sampled sibling branch was a stale pre-merge snapshot or already-merged content, consistent with every prior same-day iteration). Per AGENT_PROTOCOL's empty-backlog priority order, the highest-leverage remaining target was a sold-capability/parity gap rather than a manufactured metric — and this is a documented-invariant gap, not an invention: AGENT_PROTOCOL states 'Every fulfillment/money due-queue on the summary-card grid carries an oldest Xh staleness signal on both dashboard and digest.' A systematic cross-check of every PipelineHealth field against its dashboard MetricCard and digest section header found openHandoffs and paidNotLive were the only two due-queues on the grid still rendering a bare count with no staleness suffix, while all ~15 siblings already comply. openHandoffs is the fulfillment-debt queue for paid sites awaiting DNS / Mark live; without an age signal an operator triaging the daily digest or dashboard cannot tell a site that went paid an hour ago from one stuck three weeks — precisely the SLA-breach/refund-risk prioritization the staleness signal exists to give. openHandoffs was chosen over paidNotLive because it has a clean, unambiguous anchor: every deploy_handoffs row carries createdAt, so 'oldest open handoff age' is well-defined for the whole set. paidNotLive's natural anchor is 'time since payment', but a lead can reach stage=paid via the dashboard stage dropdown or a CSV backfill with no order row and no stage-transition timestamp at all (the exact case that motivated createDeployHandoffForLeadAction in paid-not-live-dashboard-panel-and-remedy), so anchoring it needs a design decision (skip-if-no-order, like oldestColdLeadAgeHours skips leads with no lastOutreachAt, vs. some lead-level timestamp) deliberately left out of this narrow one-queue fix. Independently verified before shipping (not taken from either subagent, which were tasked on other tiers): grepped pipeline-health-panel.tsx and daily-digest.ts and confirmed openHandoffs/paidNotLive were the only two grid cards with no oldest-age branch; confirmed DeployHandoff.createdAt exists (src/lib/deploy/types.ts:48) and that the digest already filters+sorts openHandoffsAll by createdAt ASC so the oldest is trivially available; confirmed formatAbandonedAgeHours was already imported in the panel (no new import) so this is purely additive. Tests: pipeline-health.test.ts extended makeHandoff to take Partial<DeployHandoff> overrides (mirroring makeInquiry) and added a case asserting oldestOpenHandoffAgeHours = 40 across two open handoffs while a 500h-old LIVE row is correctly ignored, plus null when none open; daily-digest.test.ts added an assertion to the existing 'lists open production handoffs' test (oldest open = 100h, older live row skipped) and asserted the rendered header reads 'Production handoffs open (1 · oldest 60h)'. Verified: npm test (2125 passed, 166 files = prior 2124 baseline + 1 net-new pipeline-health case; the digest changes tightened assertions on existing tests rather than adding files) + npm run lint (clean) + npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run build (tsc clean, all 31 routes generated) + npm run dev sanity check: curled /dashboard/leads, /preview/demo-cafe, /docs/process (all 200; the 'Open deploy handoffs' card renders and the only 'error' substrings in the dashboard HTML are Next.js's own error.tsx/global-error.tsx boundary chunks), then stopped the dev server and confirmed port 3000 free.",
