    rationale:
      "Resolves the design question open-deploy-handoff-staleness-signal deliberately deferred: what anchors 'time since payment' for a stage=paid lead with no order row (dashboard stage dropdown or CSV backfill, no Stripe checkout involved)? Read src/lib/leads/types.ts directly before assuming an answer — Lead has no createdAt, no updatedAt, and no stage-transition timestamp of any kind, only outreach/preview/snooze-specific ISO fields tied to distinct features. Forcing an anchor onto a nonexistent field (e.g. silently treating 'now' as the payment time) would have hidden real fulfillment debt behind a fake zero-age reading — worse than no signal at all — so per this iteration's instructions ('if there's truly no usable timestamp, don't force it'), the fix instead follows the established skip-if-no-order precedent already used three times in this codebase (oldestColdLeadAgeHours skips a lead with no lastOutreachAt; oldestMarketingPacksDueAgeHours / oldestStarterUpsellCandidateAgeHours skip a candidate with no qualifying order): a paid-not-live lead that does carry a bundle order (the common case — the Stripe webhook is what usually sets stage=paid in the first place) anchors the signal on that order's createdAt; a lead with no order at all (the CSV-backfill/stage-dropdown edge case) is excluded from the age computation but stays fully counted in paidNotLiveCount, exactly like a lastOutreachAt-less cold lead stays counted in coldLeadCount. This is a real, non-fake answer to a real open question, not a manufactured metric — the free NEXT_STEPS backlog stayed fully gated (stripe-price-objects / lead-ingestion / marketing-content-scheduling / commerce-payouts-stripe-connect / github-actions-runner-unavailable), and PR #428's own body named this as the next queued half of the sold-capability three-surface pattern. Independently re-verified before implementing: read src/lib/leads/types.ts end-to-end (confirmed no usable field); read src/lib/billing/starter-upsell.ts's oldestStarterUpsellCandidateAgeHours and src/lib/marketing/monthly-pack.ts's oldestMarketingPacksDueAgeHours as the direct precedent for the skip-if-no-order shape (candidate-slug Set, iterate orders, skip non-candidates and unparseable createdAt, track the minimum createdAtMs = maximum age); confirmed OrderRecord carries leadSlug + createdAt (src/lib/orders/types.ts) with no filtering needed by tier/refunded/disputed since paidNotLiveCount itself applies no such filter either — consistency over inventing a stricter subset. Deliberately left leads-client.tsx's per-lead paid-not-live panel untouched: the sibling openHandoffs fix stayed scoped to pipeline-health.ts + daily-digest.ts + the MetricCard hint only, so this fix stays symmetric with that precedent instead of scope-creeping into new per-lead UI in the same iteration. Tests: pipeline-health.test.ts added a direct describe block for oldestPaidNotLiveAgeHours (empty candidates, no matching order, unparseable/missing createdAt, oldest-across-candidates selection ignoring a non-candidate's older order, future-createdAt clamped to 0) plus wiring assertions inside computePipelineHealth (paidNotLiveCount unaffected by an orderless lead; a live lead's older order must not anchor the paid-not-live signal). daily-digest.test.ts added a wiring test (oldest matching order across two paid-not-live leads with a third orderless lead present) and two HTML-rendering tests (no order → header has no ' · oldest' suffix; with order → 'Paid, not yet live (1 · oldest 60h)'). Verified: npm test (2133 passed, 166 files = prior 2125 baseline + 8 new, all in pipeline-health.test.ts/daily-digest.test.ts) + npm run lint (clean) + npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run build (tsc clean, all 31 routes generated) + npm run dev sanity check: curled /, /dashboard/leads, /preview/demo-cafe, /docs/process (all 200; grepped the dashboard HTML for 'Paid, not live' — renders — and for error-boundary markers — none), then stopped the dev server and confirmed port 3000 free.",
