      "This iteration's baseline (npm ci fresh + tsc/lint/test/build all green, 2293 tests/174 files/34 routes) matched the just-merged clean-audit-checkout-parity-entitlement-security-review tip exactly. Fold-scan found only origin/main and this branch on the remote (no live sibling to fold) and PR #202 remained the same weeks-stale unrelated draft. Per AGENT_PROTOCOL's empty-backlog priority order, dispatched a read-only research agent explicitly primed with the full AGENT_PROTOCOL text and told which ground the last ~20 iterations had already exhaustively re-confirmed clean (tier 1 landing-page series explicitly closed; tier 2 Convex/SQLite parity re-verified multiple times including this exact commit range; tier 3 CSP/headers/rate-limiting/escaping/redirect-validation all covered; tier 4 every payment module has direct test coverage; tier 5 docs gaps already closed) — instructed to cast a genuinely wide net rather than re-tread that ground. It found this bug by tracing the actual refund.updated code path end to end (src/app/api/stripe/webhook/route.ts ~line 1864 backed by refundStatusReversesRefund in src/lib/payments/refunds.ts) rather than pattern-matching on file names, and correctly identified it as the same anti-pattern AGENT_PROTOCOL's Stripe-webhook-fulfillment rule already forbids elsewhere ('never by Stripe status alone... re-prove against live state') just unaddressed for this specific event. Verified the gap directly before fixing: grepped for any existing re-verification against charge.amount_refunded in the refund.updated branch (zero hits) and confirmed route.test.ts's existing reversal describe block (`refund.updated reversed-refund resolution`) only ever mocked single-refund scenarios, with no test asserting refundedAt stays set when the charge still shows a live refund. Fix shipped: refundChargeId (src/lib/payments/refunds.ts, mirrors the existing chargePaymentIntentId extraction pattern for a refund's `charge` field, string-or-expanded-object); the webhook handler now retrieves the charge and calls chargeHasRefund on it before the existing session-lookup/clear logic, breaking out (no-op, idempotent) whenever the charge still shows amount_refunded > 0; a new WebhookFulfillmentStep (`commerce_order_refund_reversed_charge_lookup`) so a transient Stripe API failure on this new re-verification call correctly 5xxs for Stripe retry rather than silently skipping the check. AGENT_PROTOCOL's dispute/refund lifecycle bullet extended with the general lesson (a reversal/closed-twin handler keyed on a single sub-object event's own status is not ground truth when the parent object can have multiple independent sub-objects — re-fetch and re-check the parent's own aggregate field). Added direct test coverage in the exact style of the sibling refund.updated tests: refundChargeId unit tests (refunds.test.ts, string/object/null/blank cases mirroring chargePaymentIntentId's own suite), a new WebhookFulfillmentStep test (webhook-fulfillment.test.ts), and three new route.test.ts cases in the existing 'refund.updated reversed-refund resolution' describe block — the key regression test simulates exactly the two-refund sequence from the bug report (retrieveCharge resolves amount_refunded: 3000, simulating a still-live earlier refund) and asserts clearCommerceOrderRefunded/clearOrderRefunded are never called and the session lookup never even runs; plus a no-charge-on-the-event skip case and a charge-retrieve-failure 500 case. The default mock for the new stripe.charges.retrieve call resolves amount_refunded: 0 so every pre-existing reversal test (which assumed no other live refund) keeps passing unchanged.",
