    id: "cold-lead-disposition-paid-live-race-guard",
    decision:
      "applyColdLeadDisposition (convex/leads.ts's applyColdDisposition mutation and its SQLite twin in src/lib/db.ts) now atomically re-checks the fresh row's stage against paid/live immediately before patching, returning false (no write applied) when a concurrent payment already moved the lead — instead of trusting disposeColdLeadAction's earlier planColdLeadDisposition snapshot check alone. Both functions changed return type from void/null to boolean; disposeColdLeadAction captures it and returns a specific 'refresh and check its status' error (skipping any Email 1 send) rather than silently reporting success on a write that never applied.",
    rationale:
      "Dispatched two parallel research agents on the empty-backlog fallback order: one for tier 1 (sold-capability wiring gaps), one for tiers 2-3 (Convex/SQLite parity/idempotency + security/injection), each explicitly primed with everything the prior ~17 consecutive audit passes had already covered (markCommerceOrderPaidOutAction's refund/dispute/paid-out race, replyToInquiryAction's archive race, deploy handoff provision lost-update, orphan Stripe product archive lost-update, catalog sync lost-update, refund-reversal charge-aggregate recheck, preview-open clock-skew guard, the full security/CSP/rate-limit/redirect-validation series) so they would not re-tread ground. The tier-2 agent found a live instance of the exact same action-vs-mutation TOCTOU shape as markPaidOut and recordReply, in a write path neither of those two prior fixes had swept: disposeColdLeadAction (src/app/dashboard/leads/actions.ts) reads a lead snapshot once via getLeadBySlug, computes a Re-engage/Close patch via planColdLeadDisposition — which only rejects on that STALE snapshot's stage already being paid/live — then calls applyColdLeadDisposition, whose Convex mutation (convex/leads.ts applyColdDisposition) and SQLite fallback (src/lib/db.ts) both patched stage/outreachStep/lastOutreachAt/snoozedUntil unconditionally, with zero re-check at write time of the very field the action's gate had already inspected on a now-stale copy.\n\nIndependently re-verified before implementing (not trusted as reported): read convex/leads.ts's applyColdDisposition handler directly (unconditional ctx.db.patch(lead._id, {...}), no stage check) and src/lib/db.ts's applyColdLeadDisposition SQLite fallback directly (UPDATE leads SET status = ?, ... WHERE slug = ?, no WHERE-clause guard beyond the slug), confirmed planColdLeadDisposition's paid/live rejection (src/lib/leads/cold-archive.ts) only ever sees the caller's earlier read, and confirmed leadEligibleForMarketingPack / leadEligibleForCommerceCatalog / the Starter-upsell eligibility predicates all gate purely on lead.stage — so a lost update here is a real revenue-integrity bug, not a cosmetic one: an operator clicking Close on a cold lead while, in that same read-write window, the same lead's prospect completes a genuine Stripe checkout via an old outreach link (recordLeadPayment commits stage='paid' first) would have the cold-disposition write silently revert stage back to closed/discovered, stripping a paying customer's marketing/voice/Commerce eligibility with no operator-visible error (the action still reported success:true). Confirmed applyColdLeadDisposition has exactly the one real call site (disposeColdLeadAction), so the void/null-to-boolean return-type change is fully scoped and non-breaking, matching the precedent markPaidOut already set for this exact class of signature change.\n\nFixed by making the paid/live guard atomic with the write on both backends, mirroring commerce-order-paid-out-refund-race-guard's shape exactly: convex/leads.ts's applyColdDisposition now returns false without patching when the freshly-read row's stage is already 'paid' or 'live', true after actually patching; src/lib/db.ts's applyColdLeadDisposition SQLite fallback re-reads status alongside slug in its existing existence-check query and returns false the same way, still throwing 'Lead with slug ... not found' when the row is genuinely missing (unchanged — the lead-write-not-found-parity structural guard locks that throw shape and does not need updating, since the throw-before-write pattern itself was untouched). disposeColdLeadAction now captures the boolean and, on false, returns 'Lead was paid or went live after this page loaded — refresh and check its status; the cold-lead disposition was not applied' before ever reaching the Email 1 send-on-reengage branch, so a lost race can no longer also fire a stray outreach email against a customer who just paid.\n\nAdded convex/leads.test.ts coverage: a clean-lead case asserting applied=true and the patch lands, plus two new race-guard cases (fresh row already 'paid', and separately already 'live') asserting applied=false with the row's stage/outreachStep left untouched — same call shape as commerce-order-paid-out-refund-race-guard's three-case regression test. Extended dispose-cold-lead-action.test.ts with two new cases: applyColdLeadDisposition resolving false on a bare Close, and the same false result on a Re-engage + sendEmail1 call, both asserting the new error message and that recordLeadOutreach/sendOutreachEmail/revalidatePath are never reached.\n\nDeferred in the same pass rather than shipped: the tier-1 research agent's finding (commerceOrders.clientReceiptEmailSentAt has no pipeline-health/digest/dashboard visibility and no manual resend action) was independently judged lower business severity than this active revenue-integrity race and left as NEXT_STEPS/BUSINESS_DECISIONS entry commerce-buy-now-client-receipt-visibility (status=todo, no owner) for a future iteration rather than bundled into an unrelated fix or fake-completed.\n\nVerified: npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run lint (clean) + npx vitest run convex/leads.test.ts src/app/dashboard/leads/dispose-cold-lead-action.test.ts (35 passed) + npm test (2315 passed, 174 files = 2310 baseline + 5 new) + npm run build (clean, same 34-route ○/ƒ split). Directly exercised the shipped SQLite guard against a real local.db via node:sqlite (this sandbox has no NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL configured, so the SQLite fallback is the live path here): inserted a lead row with status='paid', ran the exact guard logic now shipped in applyColdLeadDisposition against a Close attempt, confirmed it returned applied=false with the row's status/outreachStep completely untouched; inserted a second, genuinely cold (outreach_sent) lead row and confirmed the identical code path still applies normally (applied=true, status written to 'closed'). Also ran a real npm run dev pass: curled /, /dashboard, /dashboard/leads, /preview/demo-cafe, /docs/process (all 200) before and after the guard exercise; deleted both inserted test rows afterward and confirmed zero leftover rows, then stopped the dev server and confirmed port 3000 free.",
