    decision:
      "sendFollowUpAction (src/app/dashboard/leads/actions.ts, the operator Email 2/3 follow-up send) checked lead.stage against a snapshot read at the top of the action, then called recordLeadOutreach and sent a real Resend email without ever re-checking that snapshot at write time — a concurrent Stripe checkout completing (or another operator changing stage) in that window let a genuine Email 2/3 marketing follow-up fire at a customer who had just paid, gone live, or been closed, directly contradicting the action's own stated invariant, while still returning success:true with no operator visibility into the miss. Fixed by making recordOutreach (convex/leads.ts) and its SQLite fallback recordLeadOutreach (src/lib/db.ts) atomically re-check the fresh row's stage at write time and return a boolean (false = paid/live/closed, patch skipped), mirroring applyColdDisposition's existing race-guard shape exactly; sendFollowUpAction now bails with an operator-visible error and skips the Resend send entirely when the write comes back false.",
    rationale:
      "Picked up as a scheduled routine continuing this backlog after PR #496 (commerce-buy-now-client-receipt-visibility-shipped, tip of main at 6f1c454). NEXT_STEPS was back to fully gated (the same five operator/legal/infra-blocked items) with no free todo, so dispatched a research agent on the empty-backlog tier order; it found this gap and I independently re-verified before touching anything: read sendFollowUpAction (actions.ts:930-1027) in full, confirmed recordOutreach's Convex handler (convex/leads.ts) patched outreachStep/lastOutreachAt unconditionally once the row existed with no stage check anywhere in the function body, and confirmed the SQLite fallback recordLeadOutreach (src/lib/db.ts) had the identical shape — an existence check only, no stage re-check. Grepped the full prompt_process.tsx for 'sendFollowUpAction', 'recordOutreach', and 'Email 2/3' and confirmed no prior entry covers this specific write path — every existing TOCTOU race-guard entry in this exact codebase (markPaidOut, replyToInquiry's recordReply, applyColdDisposition) covers a different mutation.\n\nThis is the fourth instance of this exact bug class in this repo (markCommerceOrderPaidOutAction → commerce-order-paid-out-refund-race-guard, replyToInquiryAction → inquiry-reply-archive-race-guard, disposeColdLeadAction → cold-lead-disposition-paid-live-race-guard, now sendFollowUpAction) — followed the established fix shape exactly rather than inventing a new pattern: convex/leads.ts's recordOutreach mutation's `returns` changed from v.null() to v.boolean(), gained a `lead.stage === \"paid\" || \"live\" || \"closed\"` guard returning false before the patch (mirroring applyColdDisposition's paid/live check, extended to closed since that is also a race target sendFollowUpAction's own top-of-function gate already treats as terminal); src/lib/db.ts's recordLeadOutreach return type changed from Promise<void> to Promise<boolean>, the Convex branch returns the mutation's boolean, and the SQLite fallback now selects status alongside slug in its existing existence check and returns false (no UPDATE) when status is already paid/live/closed. sendFollowUpAction captures the boolean and returns 'Lead was paid, went live, or was closed after this page loaded — refresh and check its status; the follow-up was not sent' before reaching the Resend send, mirroring disposeColdLeadAction's error-message convention. Left recordLeadOutreach's other two call sites (updateLeadStageAction's Email-1-on-stage-change branch, disposeColdLeadAction's Email-1-on-re-engage branch, addLeadAction's Email-1-on-create branch) with the return value uncaptured and unchanged: all three call it immediately after their own write already set/confirmed a non-terminal stage in the same action (updateLeadStageAction just wrote outreach_sent; disposeColdLeadAction's applyColdLeadDisposition already atomically proved the row was not paid/live moments earlier; addLeadAction just created the row), so the marginal race window is negligible and out of scope for this pass — matching this file's existing precedent of only fixing the read-then-write-without-recheck action, not every call site of a shared helper.\n\nVerified: npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors, confirming the two other ignored call sites still compile with the new boolean return type) + npm run lint (clean) + npx vitest run convex/leads.test.ts src/app/dashboard/leads/send-follow-up-action.test.ts (33 passed, adding one new Convex race-guard test covering paid/live/closed and one new action-level test) + npm test (2322 passed, 174 files = 2320 baseline + 2 new) + npm run build (clean, same 34-route ○/ƒ split). Real npm run dev pass beyond a curl-for-200 check, since this bug class is specifically about a race window invisible to a status-code check: on a fresh local.db, ran the exact shipped SQLite guard function directly against a real inserted lead row with status='paid' and confirmed it returned false with outreachStep/lastOutreachAt left completely untouched, then flipped the same row to a cold stage and confirmed the identical guard code path applied normally (returned true, outreachStep/lastOutreachAt written) — proving both the reject and accept branches against a real database, not just mocks; also curled /, /dashboard, /dashboard/leads, /preview/demo-cafe, /docs/process (all 200) before and after; deleted the inserted test row afterward, confirmed zero leftover rows, then stopped the dev server and confirmed port 3000 free.",
