      "commerceOrders.markClientReceiptSent (both backends) now atomically re-checks clientReceiptEmailSentAt at write time instead of patching unconditionally — the seventh instance of the action-vs-mutation TOCTOU lost-update class this repo has fixed, found in the one durable-marker mutation in convex/commerceOrders.ts that was missing the guard every sibling (markPaidOut, markRefunded, markDisputed) already has.",
    rationale:
      "Picked up as a scheduled routine (\"continue toward a profitable, growing business\") after PR #502 (preview-page-rate-limit, tip of main at 695f198); this branch (claude/upbeat-dijkstra-5qcz8s) was already at that exact tip on the remote. Confirmed baseline green: fresh npm ci + npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run lint (clean) + npm test (176 files / 2351 passed) + npm run build (clean, same 34-route split). NEXT_STEPS confirmed still fully gated via direct grep (exactly five status=\"todo\" entries, unchanged: stripe-price-objects, lead-ingestion, marketing-content-scheduling, commerce-payouts-stripe-connect, github-actions-runner-unavailable). Fold-scanned the remote: ranked the ~30 most-recently-pushed branches by commit timestamp and rev-list-counted each against origin/main — every one showed ahead<=1, and the two outliers (claude/upbeat-dijkstra-v2iugu, claude/nice-euler-0dj8uo) were diffed directly and confirmed to be the same already-merged content (PR #499's commit and an earlier docs-process entry respectively) under different hashes from stale fork points — no live fold candidate. mcp__github__list_pull_requests confirmed the one open PR (#202) is still the same weeks-stale unrelated draft every prior iteration has noted.\n\nDispatched a research agent primed with the full AGENT_PROTOCOL text, the tier 1-5 empty-backlog fallback order, and the last five closed ITERATIONS entries so it would not re-propose an eighth trivial variant of the paid/live/closed race class already swept exhaustively across actions.ts. It read every mutation in convex/commerceOrders.ts side by side and found markClientReceiptSent was the sole outlier: markPaidOut/markRefunded/markDisputed/clearRefunded/clearDisputed all re-check their own gating field before patching, but markClientReceiptSent (added when commerce-buy-now-client-receipt-visibility-shipped/manual-resend landed) patched unconditionally with returns: v.null(), and its SQLite twin markCommerceOrderClientReceiptSent in db.ts ran a bare UPDATE with no WHERE-clause guard and Promise<void>. Both live callers — resendCommerceClientReceiptAction (operator manual resend) and the Stripe webhook's redelivery-recovery branch — read clientReceiptEmailSentAt, send the email, then call this mutation; an operator resend racing a webhook redelivery (or two redeliveries) can both pass their own stale-unset read and both send, and the unconditional patch gave no signal that a race occurred.\n\nIndependently re-verified before touching anything: read markClientReceiptSent's full handler (unconditional ctx.db.patch, no order.clientReceiptEmailSentAt check) and its SQLite twin (bare UPDATE ... WHERE stripeSessionId = ? with no second predicate) side by side against markPaidOut's atomic refundedAt/disputedAt/paidOutAt re-check; read both call sites end-to-end (actions.ts lines ~1405-1500, the webhook route's runClientReceipt branch) and confirmed neither has any shared lock between its read and its write; grepped convex/commerceOrders.test.ts and confirmed no test exercised a repeat-mark race for this mutation, unlike markPaidOut's dedicated race-guard test.\n\nShipped the same fix shape as the six prior instances (most recently checkout-session-recovery-race-guard): markClientReceiptSent's returns changed from v.null() to v.boolean(); guards on `!order || order.clientReceiptEmailSentAt` before patching, returns whether it actually applied. markCommerceOrderClientReceiptSent's return type changed from Promise<void> to Promise<boolean>; the Convex branch returns the mutation's boolean; the SQLite UPDATE gained `AND (clientReceiptEmailSentAt IS NULL OR clientReceiptEmailSentAt = '')` and returns result.changes > 0. resendCommerceClientReceiptAction now captures that boolean and, on false, returns a distinct 'already marked sent by a concurrent request — this click may have sent a duplicate notification email' error instead of silently reporting success. The webhook's marker call now captures the boolean too, but — unlike the action — treats false as a non-fatal console.warn rather than a fulfillment failure: the persisted state is already consistent (marked sent by whichever writer won the race), so there is nothing for Stripe to usefully retry; only a thrown/rejected write (the pre-existing catch block, unchanged) still 5xxs.\n\nTest coverage: convex/commerceOrders.test.ts gained two cases mirroring markPaidOut's race-guard test — a race where the second call loses and the row keeps the first-recorded timestamp (never last-writer-wins clobbered), and an unknown-stripeSessionId safe no-op returning false. resend-commerce-client-receipt-action.test.ts's beforeEach default changed from mockResolvedValue(undefined) to mockResolvedValue(true), plus one new case asserting the duplicate-risk error and that revalidatePath is skipped when the mutation returns false. route.test.ts's default changed the same way, plus one new case asserting a false return still yields HTTP 200 (not a fulfillment failure).\n\nVerified: npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run lint (clean) + npx vitest run convex/commerceOrders.test.ts src/app/dashboard/leads/resend-commerce-client-receipt-action.test.ts src/app/api/stripe/webhook/route.test.ts (202 passed) + npm test (2355 passed, 176 files = 2351 baseline + 4 new) + npm run build (clean, same 34-route ○/ƒ split). Real verification beyond build/lint/test, since this bug class is invisible to status codes: ran the exact shipped guarded SQLite UPDATE directly against a throwaway database, confirming a first write applies (changes=1) and an immediate racing second write is rejected (changes=0) with the original timestamp left intact — then repeated the identical check against the actual dev-server local.db (inserted a real commerce_orders row against the example-bakery lead, confirmed it rendered in /dashboard/leads's 'Missing client receipt' section, ran the guarded UPDATE twice to reproduce accept-then-reject against that real row, then deleted the row and confirmed zero leftover rows). Also curled /, /dashboard/leads, /preview/demo-cafe, /docs/process (all 200) with the dev server up, then stopped it and confirmed port 3000 free. NEXT_STEPS: unchanged (all five gated items stayed as-is) — this is a race-condition bug fix on already-shipped code, not a new backlog item.",
