      "All 100+ prior empty-backlog iterations optimized code-invariant correctness (schema parity, security, idempotency, dead code, docs accuracy) — none built a new organic customer-acquisition surface, even though lead-ingestion (the primary planned lead-source channel) is legal-gated on Places API review and has been status=todo since before this file's tail. Shipped three static /websites-for-restaurants, /websites-for-salons, /websites-for-trades landing pages targeting long-tail local-business search queries (\"website for a restaurant\", \"salon website builder\", \"website for a plumber\") that funnel straight to the existing /checkout?tier=<recommendedTier> flow — an acquisition channel entirely buildable with content + routing, unlike Places API ingestion, and additive to (not a substitute for) it. Each page: category-specific hero/pain-points/features/FAQ copy, a live example link to the matching curated DEMO_LEADS preview (example-bakery / serene-salon / mountain-plumbing — all always-indexable per isCuratedDemoLeadSlug, so linking them from a new indexable page introduces no consent gap), the matching CATEGORY_THEMES visual theme (src/lib/previews/themes.ts) for brand consistency with the preview it links to, and its own generateMetadata + schema.org Service JSON-LD (categoryLandingServiceJsonLd, src/lib/seo.ts) — FAQPage JSON-LD was deliberately not used, per the same Google rich-result-eligibility reasoning homepage-organization-jsonld already recorded. Single source of truth: src/lib/marketing/category-landing.ts (CATEGORY_LANDING_PAGES), consumed by all three page.tsx files, src/app/sitemap.ts (STATIC_ROUTES, priority 0.9 alongside /checkout — same conversion tier, ranked above informational /docs at 0.5), and a new homepage \"Built for your industry\" section (src/app/page.tsx) linking all three — mirrors the DOCS_PAGES single-source-of-truth pattern that fixed sitemap-docs-route-sync, so a future fourth category landing page can't ship indexable-but-unlisted the same way 9/12 docs pages once did.",
    rationale:
      "AGENT_PROTOCOL's empty-backlog priority order (fold > sold-capability wiring > Convex/SQLite parity > security > untested orchestration > docs clarity) is itself scoped to code-invariant maintenance on an already-shipped product — it has no entry for 'build a new growth lever,' because until now every iteration correctly found the free backlog exhausted at that scope. Re-reading this iteration's actual mandate (get the business itself profitable and growing, not just keep the codebase clean) surfaced a gap the priority order doesn't cover: revenue growth needs either more leads into the funnel or better conversion of existing traffic, and lead-ingestion — the one NEXT_STEPS item that would add lead volume — is legal-gated indefinitely. Organic search traffic converting directly at /checkout is a channel an agent can build unassisted, so it's a legitimate, non-manufactured addition to the standing priority list rather than an invented busywork metric (the AGENT_PROTOCOL anti-pattern this decision is careful not to fall into: this ships a real, indexable, functionally complete page users can act on today, not a speculative aggregate no one reads). Deliberately scoped to 3 pages (one per non-generic BusinessCategory already in the data model) rather than a larger content-marketing program (blog, dozens of city/category combinations) — that scale of SEO investment needs real keyword-volume research and case-study content an agent can't fabricate credibly, and is better attempted incrementally once these three pages have real traffic data to learn from. Verified: 8 new Vitest cases (category-landing.test.ts data-integrity checks — unique hrefs, recommendedTier resolves to a real bundle, exampleLeadSlug resolves to a real curated demo lead in the matching category; seo.test.ts categoryLandingPageMetadata/categoryLandingServiceJsonLd; sitemap.test.ts route-sync) + npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run lint (clean, one react/no-unescaped-entities fix) + npm test (2445 passed = 2437 baseline + 8 new, 185 files) + a full clean rebuild (`rm -rf .next && npm run build`, clean, 3 new ○ static routes, same ƒ/○ split otherwise) + npm run dev sanity check: curled /, /websites-for-restaurants, /websites-for-salons, /websites-for-trades, /sitemap.xml (all 200), grepped each landing page's rendered HTML for its title tag, Service JSON-LD block, category-correct checkout tier link, and live-example preview link (all present and correct), grepped the homepage for the new cross-links, grepped /sitemap.xml for all three new routes; stopped the dev server, confirmed port 3000 refused connections, and deleted local.db afterward. NEXT_STEPS unchanged (all five gated items stayed as-is) — this is a new organic-acquisition surface, not a resolution of any gated item; fold-scan of the newest 5 remote branches at session start found zero live candidates (all product-diff-empty against origin/main); sole open PR still #202 (same weeks-stale unrelated draft); GitHub Actions runner outage reconfirmed unresolved (recent sampled runs still conclusion=failure, no runner assigned) — still operator-side, no new information; no live Stripe/Resend/Convex/Anthropic secret in this session's environment either, so stripe-price-objects stays the sole revenue-blocking gated item.",
